# Find a view of the checkerboard, by sweeping until one detects.
#
# Per (camera, direction): sweep zoom with small pitch/yaw nudges on a
# low-resolution anypoint until the board is found, then re-run the detection at
# full resolution and report the winning angles for the dialog's spin boxes.
#
# It is a search, so it is an action -- tens of low-res remaps, each a full
# per-pixel transform, and the operator gets to stop it.
string camera
string direction

# The board's inner-corner counts, as the operator typed them. 0 x 0 means "no
# hint": the search then tries square boards from 4x4 to 9x9.
#
# A typed size is a HINT, not a constraint. The search also tries its transpose
# and its count-1 -- the second because typing SQUARES instead of inner corners is
# the commonest mistake here, and it produces a board that never detects with no
# indication why.
int32 pattern_cols
int32 pattern_rows

# Where to search from: the direction's current angles. The preset for a direction
# is a starting point, not the answer -- an off-centre optical axis or an
# off-centre board puts the real one degrees away, which is what stage A pans for.
float64 base_pitch
float64 base_yaw
float64 base_zoom
---
bool success

# The view that worked. The client writes these into the spin boxes; it does not
# derive them.
float64 alpha
float64 beta
float64 theta
float64 zoom

bool found
bool cancelled

# The board size the search actually detected, which is NOT always the one that
# was asked for -- it may be the transpose, or count-1 when the operator typed
# squares. The client writes these back into the direction's size field, because
# a later manual Detect at the winning angles with the WRONG size finds nothing
# and looks like the auto-frame lied.
int32 pattern_cols
int32 pattern_rows

# The full-resolution detection at the winning angles, same shape as
# DetectCheckerboard's -- so a successful auto-frame leaves the direction
# detected, not merely aimed.
string detection_json
sensor_msgs/CompressedImage overlay

string message
---
int32 done
int32 total
float64 zoom       # what it is trying right now, so the sweep is visible
string stage
